#      only with a line in the vault inventory saying so. This is noise
#      reduction, never risk acceptance.
#   2. NEVER add a fingerprint to make a scan pass. If a new finding appears,
#      rotate it and write it down; the file is not a snooze button.
#   3. This is fingerprints, not paths. A `paths` allowlist in .gitleaks.toml
#      matches in every scan mode and would blind history scans to everything a
#      path ever held (see the comment at the bottom of .gitleaks.toml). A
#      fingerprint pins one finding in one commit and cannot over-reach.
#   4. Delete the entries for a file once filter-repo has removed the blobs —
#      a stale fingerprint is a claim that something was checked when it wasn't.
